    <string name="ios_style_dynamic_island_android">An iOS-style Dynamic Island for Android. It draws a floating pill near the camera cutout and lets live activities — music, notifications, charging, timers, privacy indicators — take it over, one at a time, by priority.</string>
    <string name="how_island_decides_what_show">How the island decides what to show</string>
    <string name="notifications_outrank_everything_then_privacy">Notifications outrank everything, then privacy, unlock, volume, ringer, battery.</string>
    <string name="music_timers_are_sticky_they">Music and timers are sticky: they stay until playback stops or the timer ends.</string>
    <string name="anything_transient_fades_back_resting">Anything transient fades back to the resting pill once its time is up.</string>
    <string name="why_can_sit_top_status">Why it can\'t sit on top of the status bar</string>
    <string name="android_layers_windows_by_type">Android layers windows by type. An app overlay — the only kind an app without system privileges can create — is always placed below the status bar, and the status bar consumes every touch inside its own band. No permission, flag or window type changes that for a normal app.</string>
    <string name="over_status_bar_done_by">So \"over the status bar\" is done by drawing, not by layering. In Look → Position → Over the status bar the island is drawn up at the cutout, where it reads as part of the hardware, and a transparent strip hangs just below the status bar to catch taps. Centre it and the system clock and icons sit either side of it rather than through it.</string>
    <string name="anything_genuinely_draws_above_status">Anything that genuinely draws above the status bar is a system app, a launcher, or a build with elevated privileges.</string>
    <string name="keeping_alive">Keeping it alive</string>
    <string name="android_may_stop_background_overlays">Android may stop background overlays on aggressive battery settings. Excluding Notch Island from battery optimisation keeps it steady.</string>
